            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 57-year-old female patient, admitted on 03/06/2003 with acute lower abdominal pain and suspected tubal pregnancy. On admission, physical examination revealed peritoneal signs. Transvaginal ultrasonography confirmed an ectopic tubal pregnancy with signs of early rupture. Serum beta-hCG was markedly elevated. Given the clinical findings and hemodynamic status, the decision was made for surgical intervention. The patient underwent laparoscopic salpingectomy for tubal ectopic pregnancy, which was performed without complications. Postoperative recovery was uneventful. Wound care was provided and vital signs remained stable throughout. The patient was discharged home on 04/06/2003 in good general condition. Follow-up including beta-hCG monitoring and contraceptive counseling is recommended. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
